From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: smit1237 <smit1237@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 22:47:49 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 09/30] portal: rnsbox-portal C++/CGI admin UI (uhttpd)

A single riscv64 C++/CGI binary served per-request by uhttpd (OpenWrt's
tiny HTTP server), replacing the former Flask app so the web tier keeps
~0 resident RAM (no long-lived interpreter). Pages are server-rendered
from .html templates under /usr/share/rnsbox-portal/pages in a shared
OpenWrt-style chrome; POST forms use POST-redirect-GET with a one-shot
flash cookie. Session auth is werkzeug-compatible pbkdf2 (libcrypto).
nftables generation (single source of truth for the UI and the boot
scripts) is the binary's `nftgen` CLI mode.

uhttpd replaces busybox httpd: it serves the docroot index at bare "/"
(busybox httpd 404s it), follows the /www/cgi-bin/portal symlink to the
extensionless CGI, and does proper redirects/error pages.
